    "created_at": "2024-03-13T20:07:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-13T20:07:42Z",
    "body": "Thank you all for attending this meeting! Here are the notes from this meeting (the next one is at https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10200):\r\n\r\n### Agenda  \r\nAttendees: Luke Warlow, Michael Smith, Marcos Caceres, Dan Clark, Chris Harrelson, Brian Kardell, Vladimir Levin, Olli Pettay, Michael Riley, Chris Wilson, Stephanie Zhang, Domenic Denicola, Johnny Stenback\r\n\r\n1. Review past action items\r\n    1. Marcos or Anne will follow up with heycam on WebKit's opinion on [Add a layer and filter interface in the 2D canvas](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9537).\r\n        1. Marcos pinged with no response, will ping again; Domenic offered further detail to ask.\r\n        1. Need technical tiebreaker opinions on [https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8476#issuecomment-1826735392](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8476#issuecomment-1826735392) \r\n        1. Need general confirmation that WebKit is happy with the PR API shape. There is general WebKit interest in the feature as of [https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8476#issuecomment-1306552408](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8476#issuecomment-1306552408) \r\n    1. The Steering Group will add the `stage-1 `label to the [Stylable `<select>` element](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9799) issue after they publish the stages process.\r\n        1. Done.\r\n    1. Addison will update the [add support for internationalized email addresses](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5799) PR with the provided feedback.\r\n        1. deferred\r\n    1. Panos will file an issue with the meeting cadence change for broader visibility.\r\n        1. Filed at [https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10163](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10163), slight change suggested by dbaron to rotation, expect Panos to implement starting next week - suggestion to have next week be a Europe + America (9:00 California time) to overlap with CSS to discuss pseudoelement syntax (see below)\r\n1. Carryovers from last time\r\n    1. Joint session with the I18N WG ([tagged issues](https://github.com/w3c/i18n-activity/labels/Agenda%2BI18N%2BWHATWG)) carryover\r\n        1. Time-related issues ([#9542](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9542), [#5488](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5488))\r\n            1. Michael Riley discussed value of i18n date - Domenic asked for implementer interest, and what i18n WG perspective is.  Olli: might be nice; need to ask for detail.  Domenic points Michael to new proposals; \r\n        1. Bidi-related issues\r\n    1. [Dominic] [Atomic move operation for element reparenting & reordering](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1255)\r\n        1. Deferred\r\n    1. [Emilio] [Render-blocking: the definition of \"created by its node document's parser\" is a little bit vague](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10145)\r\n        1. Deferred\r\n    1. [Sanket] [New attribute to control UA-provided writing assistance](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9065)\r\n        1. Dan Clark: allowing authors to suppress writing assistance.  Feedback from Anne; may not be readable; haven't gotten feedback from Anne in PR.  Marcos pinging Anne to get response and unblock.\r\n1. New topics\r\n    1. [ChrisH/Domenic] [Design pattern for naming new pseudoelements](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9951) - joint issue with CSSWG.\r\n        1. To be taken up at next week's meeting?\r\n    1. [Add light dismiss functionality to `<dialog>`](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9373)\r\n        1. Luke discusses overview. Domenic mentions subtleties, encourages design and more review. Luke to check if standards-position has been filed for webkit ([done](https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/329)). Olli wonders if new attributes would be `<dialog>`-specific or could be more broadly applied.\r\n    1. [New attribute to control UA-provided writing assistance](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9065)\r\n    1. Luke gives slight nudge to talk on popover-hint.\r\n\r\n### Action Items\r\n\r\n1. @marcoscaceres or @annevk will follow up with heycam on WebKit's opinion on [Add a layer and filter interface in the 2D canvas](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9537).\r\n1. @aphillips will update the [add support for internationalized email addresses](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5799) PR with the provided feedback.\r\n1. Take up joint meeting with CSS for next week's meeting [@past]\r\n1. Ask @annevk what to do about joint issues with the I18N WG ([tagged issues](https://github.com/w3c/i18n-activity/labels/Agenda%2BI18N%2BWHATWG)) carryover, how to get i18n WG involvement, use case planning needed here.",
